# All local-only working data: runtime state (resume cursors, progress logs),
# the Steam metadata cache, and rollback snapshots. These used to be ignored
# file-by-file in the repo root, so every new state file needed a new rule and
# a missed one would commit operational state to a public repo. utils/paths.py
# puts them all under here instead, so one rule covers the lot.
_local/

# nohup fallback output. Lands in the repo root the moment a nohup command's
# redirect is mistyped, which is exactly how operational files have reached
# this public repo before. Logs belong under _local/.
nohup.out
